    "result_text": "Done. The change is implemented and all tests pass.\n\n## What I did\n\nThe spec required the owner response to include `selfLink` = `/api/owners/` + the owner's id. The acceptance test (`AcceptanceTest.coreReturnsSelfLink`) creates an owner and reads it back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`, expecting `$.selfLink` to equal `/api/owners/{id}`.\n\nFollowing the project's existing pattern for derived owner fields (which are declared in `openapi.yml` and populated by MapStruct in `OwnerMapper`), I made two edits:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `selfLink` string property to the `Owner` schema (the generated `OwnerDto`).\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a mapping that computes it:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"selfLink\",\n       expression = \"java(owner.getId() == null ? null : \\\"/api/owners/\\\" + owner.getId())\")\n   ```\n   The null guard keeps it safe for any pre-persist mapping where the id isn't assigned yet.\n\nThis flows through the existing `RespondWithOwner` responder unchanged, so both `GET /api/owners/{id}` and the create response carry the field.\n\n## Verification\n- `AcceptanceTest`: **Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0** \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.\n- Full `mvnw test` suite: green (that acceptance test is the only test class in the project).",
